{
  "channel": {
    "channel_id": "proj-eco-tourism-platform-mvp",
    "threads": [
      {
        "thread_id": "TH1",
        "thread_goal": "Align on vision, target segments, and MVP scope for the platform.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M1",
            "speaker_id": 472565,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Team, we need to get moving on the platform launch. I have put together some thoughts on the strategy. Please review the doc and let's agree on who we are targeting and what goes into the first release. We have 90 days.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "eyes",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M2",
            "speaker_id": 99087,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "I've reviewed A1. To ensure we hit the 90-day window, I recommend we narrow the target segments immediately. Based on the market research reports I analyzed, 'Eco-conscious Millennials' and 'Adventure Families' show the highest immediate demand. I've drafted the persona needs in T1. Does this align with the broader vision?",
            "mentions": [
              472565
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1",
              "T1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "heavy_plus_sign",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 22473,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "I am worried about the budget implications if we pick two segments. Maybe we should stick to one? I need to check if the current financial statements support marketing to both groups. Also, are we sure about the features list?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 185576,
            "reply_to": "M3",
            "text": "The revenue generation strategy relies on volume, so two segments are necessary to de-risk the launch. The budget is capped, but the acquisition channels overlap significantly. Regarding features, I've mapped the MVP requirements in T4 against the customer journey in A4. We should lock the feature set to 'Booking Flow', 'Partner Content', and 'Payment Processing' to stay safe.",
            "mentions": [
              22473
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T4",
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "check",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 472565,
            "reply_to": "M4",
            "text": "That sounds reasonable. If the numbers work, let's go with those segments. And yes, keep the features simple for now.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D1"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M6",
            "speaker_id": 99087,
            "reply_to": "M5",
            "text": "Great. I'm recording the decision: Primary segments are Millennials and Adventure Families (D1). MVP feature set is approved as per the strategy doc (D2). I will update the requirements doc to reflect this scope freeze.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D1",
              "D2"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "rocket",
                "count": 4
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "thread_outcome": {
          "decisions_made": [
            "D1",
            "D2"
          ],
          "next_steps": [
            {
              "task_id": "T4",
              "owner_id": 99087,
              "when": "tomorrow"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "thread_id": "TH2",
        "thread_goal": "Define and validate eco-tourism bundles, partner criteria, and service standards.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M1",
            "speaker_id": 52126,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "I have uploaded the initial draft for the eco-tourism bundles (T2) and the partner selection criteria (A3). We need to decide which specific trips make the cut for the MVP catalog. I focused on community-based tourism options.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T2",
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "palm_tree",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M2",
            "speaker_id": 263727,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "I'm looking at the list. The 'Rainforest Retreat' looks good for pricing, but the 'Mountain Trek' might be too niche for the sales targets. Can we swap it for something with broader appeal? Also, do we have the service standards ready for these?",
            "mentions": [
              52126
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 52126,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "Good point. I can replace the Trek with the 'Coastal Conservation' package. It has better cross-selling potential. For standards, I've outlined the on-site guidelines in A6. It covers safety and cultural heritage management.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A6",
              "T10"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 185576,
            "reply_to": "M3",
            "text": "The 'Coastal Conservation' package aligns better with our revenue generation strategy. Regarding the partner criteria (T6), we must ensure the compliance checklist is strict on environmental regulations to avoid liability. If A3 covers that, I'm good to approve.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T6",
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 52126,
            "reply_to": "M4",
            "text": "Yes, A3 includes the full compliance review step. So, are we agreed on the bundle list with the Coastal swap and the partner criteria?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D3",
              "D4"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "white_check_mark",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "thread_outcome": {
          "decisions_made": [
            "D3",
            "D4"
          ],
          "next_steps": [
            {
              "task_id": "T10",
              "owner_id": 52126,
              "when": "EOD"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "thread_id": "TH3",
        "thread_goal": "Lock pricing approach, financial assumptions, and budget envelope.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M1",
            "speaker_id": 472565,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "I've taken a stab at the financial model in A2. We need to agree on the pricing strategy and the overall budget envelope so I can get sign-off from the board.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2",
              "T5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M2",
            "speaker_id": 22473,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "I reviewed the sheet. The margin calculation on row 45 doesn't account for the statutory tax obligations correctly. Also, the marketing budget seems low if we want to hit the optimistic scenario. I can fix the formula errors, but we need to be careful with the assumptions.",
            "mentions": [
              472565
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "chart_with_upwards_trend",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 185576,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "Thanks for catching the tax issue. Let's adjust the pricing model to a 'premium tier' approach to cover those costs and improve the margin. For the budget envelope (T9), let's lock the base scenario figure. It gives us enough runway for the MVP build without overextending.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T9"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 472565,
            "reply_to": "M3",
            "text": "Okay, premium tier it is. And we will stick to the base budget. Can you update the risk register (T12) to reflect the budget cap?",
            "mentions": [
              185576
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T12"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D6"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 185576,
            "reply_to": "M4",
            "text": "Will do. Confirming: Pricing strategy set to Premium (D5) and Budget Envelope locked at base scenario (D6).",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5",
              "D6"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "handshake",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "thread_outcome": {
          "decisions_made": [
            "D5",
            "D6"
          ],
          "next_steps": [
            {
              "task_id": "T12",
              "owner_id": 185576,
              "when": "tomorrow"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "thread_id": "TH4",
        "thread_goal": "Prioritise backlog, define KPIs, and prepare handover to delivery teams.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M1",
            "speaker_id": 99087,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "We are approaching the build phase. I've updated the Backlog Matrix (A5) and the KPI Framework (A8). I need approval to freeze the backlog priorities so I can conduct the handover (T11).",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5",
              "A8",
              "T11"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M2",
            "speaker_id": 263727,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "The prioritization looks consistent with the sales strategy. The user stories for the booking engine are clear. I'm good with A5.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 472565,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "On the KPIs... do we have something that tracks the community impact? I want to make sure we are building trust.",
            "mentions": [
              99087
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 99087,
            "reply_to": "M3",
            "text": "Yes, in T8 I defined 'Partner Net Promoter Score' and 'Local Economic Contribution' as key impact metrics. They are included in the dashboard specs.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T8"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "thumbsup",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 185576,
            "reply_to": "M4",
            "text": "The data sources for those KPIs are identified, so we are ready. Let's freeze the backlog (D7) and approve the KPI set (D8). We can schedule the handover with the dev leads.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T12"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D7",
              "D8"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "check",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "thread_outcome": {
          "decisions_made": [
            "D7",
            "D8"
          ],
          "next_steps": [
            {
              "task_id": "T11",
              "owner_id": 99087,
              "when": "tomorrow morning"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "thread_id": "TH5",
        "thread_goal": "Align on go-to-market narrative, channels, and launch milestones.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M1",
            "speaker_id": 263727,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Here is the draft Go-To-Market Plan (A7). I've outlined the channel strategy in T7. We need to confirm the launch window and the primary channels.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A7",
              "T7"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M2",
            "speaker_id": 52126,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "Just a heads up, the partners need at least 3 weeks notice before the first booking arrives. Please ensure the launch date reflects that operational constraint.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 185576,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "Understood. We will set the external launch date for 90 days from now, with a soft launch 2 weeks prior. For channels (D10), looking at the budget, we should focus on 'Direct Digital' and 'Specialist Agencies' rather than broad OTAs initially. It yields better margins.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T9"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D9",
              "D10"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 263727,
            "reply_to": "M3",
            "text": "Agreed. Direct and Agencies give us more control over the pricing. I'll lock the launch date for the 90-day mark (D9) and prioritize those two channels (D10).",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D9",
              "D10"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "rocket",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "thread_outcome": {
          "decisions_made": [
            "D9",
            "D10"
          ],
          "next_steps": [
            {
              "task_id": "T7",
              "owner_id": 263727,
              "when": "today"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}

{
  "channel": {
    "channel_id": "proj-support-portal-mvp",
    "threads": [
      {
        "thread_id": "TH1",
        "thread_goal": "Align on MVP scope, key workflows, and initial backlog for the support portal.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M1",
            "speaker_id": 337175,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Team, we have a hard stop in 21 days for the pilot. I've initialized the backlog in A3. We need to define the absolute minimum feature set today to hit this deadline.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M2",
            "speaker_id": 6869,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "I've uploaded the requirements doc A1 based on T1. Given my experience with the legacy systems here, I suggest we focus strictly on Ticket Search and Ticket Creation for the MVP. The telephony integration is risky, so let's keep that minimal.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1",
              "T1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "heavy_plus_sign",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 377231,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "That makes sense. I can pick up T2 immediately to map out the navigation for those two flows. I'll also start the frontend scaffolding for T4 using the W3C standards we discussed.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T2",
              "T4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 109718,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "I can handle the backend services for T3. I'll need to check the API documentation for the ticketing system to see if we can hit the sandbox environment.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 561396,
            "reply_to": "M3",
            "text": "I will partner with you on T4 to ensure the responsive layout works on tablets, as agents move around. I'll also keep an eye on the backlog tracking in A3.",
            "mentions": [
              377231
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T4",
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M6",
            "speaker_id": 337175,
            "reply_to": "M5",
            "text": "Excellent pace. So, are we agreed that D1 is limited to Ticket Search, Creation, and a read-only Knowledge Base? And for D2, we have the owners assigned in A3 as discussed?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D1",
              "D2"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "white_check_mark",
                "count": 4
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M7",
            "speaker_id": 6869,
            "reply_to": "M6",
            "text": "Agreed on D1 and D2. I'll finalize the requirements in A1 by EOD to match this scope.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D1",
              "D2"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          }
        ],
        "thread_outcome": {
          "decisions_made": [
            "D1",
            "D2"
          ],
          "next_steps": [
            {
              "task_id": "T1",
              "owner_id": 6869,
              "when": "EOD"
            },
            {
              "task_id": "T2",
