        "thread_id": "TH2",
        "thread_goal": "Design and finalize the waste tracking process and supporting tools.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M19",
            "speaker_id": 66412,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi team, here is the first draft of the waste tracking template and the SOP. Let me know what you think. I tried to cover everything.",
            "mentions": [
              492953,
              332110,
              412987
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1",
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M20",
            "speaker_id": 412987,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "Thanks for sharing this. I've just reviewed A2. From my experience in kitchens, a 4-page SOP is too long for daily use. We need something much simpler. I'd suggest a one-page visual guide with photos showing 'what goes where' for the main waste categories: Spoilage, Prep Waste, and Plate Waste. This will be critical for the training materials in T7.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2",
              "T7"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "eyes",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M21",
            "speaker_id": 332110,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "Looking at the A1 tracker, it's a good start. To make it more actionable for purchasing, could we add a 'Supplier' and 'Delivery Date' column? That way we can correlate spoilage directly with specific batches or suppliers, which helps us identify quality issues faster.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M22",
            "speaker_id": 66412,
            "reply_to": "M20",
            "text": "A one-page guide is a good idea, but I'm not sure how to make one. Can you help with that?",
            "mentions": [
              412987
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M23",
            "speaker_id": 412987,
            "reply_to": "M22",
            "text": "Of course. I can sketch out a template based on what I've used before and share it with you tomorrow morning. You can then finalize it.",
            "mentions": [
              66412
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "handshake",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M24",
            "speaker_id": 66412,
            "reply_to": "M21",
            "text": "Yes, I can add those columns to A1.",
            "mentions": [
              332110
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M25",
            "speaker_id": 492953,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "Thanks for the feedback everyone. This is exactly the kind of collaboration we need. Once we finalize the tracker, let's think about the A7 Executive Dashboard. For T9, I want to see three main KPIs at the top: 1) Total Waste % (by weight), 2) Cost of Waste, and 3) Guest Satisfaction Score. Are there any others we should consider essential for leadership view?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A7",
              "T9"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M26",
            "speaker_id": 332110,
            "reply_to": "M25",
            "text": "I'd suggest adding 'Waste % by Top 5 Categories'. This will show leadership where the biggest problems are and whether our targeted interventions are working. It's a level deeper than the total waste number.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M27",
            "speaker_id": 412987,
            "reply_to": "M25",
            "text": "Agreed. And maybe 'Sales of Promoted Low-Waste Items'. This connects our sales efforts directly to the program's financial goals and shows we're driving revenue, not just cutting costs.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M28",
            "speaker_id": 61317,
            "reply_to": "M25",
            "text": "The dashboard needs to be clear and easy to understand.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M29",
            "speaker_id": 492953,
            "reply_to": "M27",
            "text": "Those are both excellent additions. Let's confirm the KPIs for the executive dashboard. Decision: The A7 dashboard will feature: Total Waste %, Cost of Waste, Guest Satisfaction, Waste % by Top 5 Categories, and Sales of Promoted Low-Waste Items.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A7"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D4"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "white_check_mark",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M30",
            "speaker_id": 332110,
            "reply_to": "M24",
            "text": "Great. Once you've added the columns to A1, let's agree on the reporting cadence. I propose kitchen staff log waste daily, and the unit manager consolidates and sends a weekly summary. This balances detail with workload.",
            "mentions": [
              66412
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M31",
            "speaker_id": 412987,
            "reply_to": "M30",
            "text": "Daily logging and weekly rollup is the standard. That works perfectly.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M32",
            "speaker_id": 492953,
            "reply_to": "M30",
            "text": "Sounds like we have a plan. Let's approve the tracking process. Decision: The waste tracking template (A1, with new columns) is approved. The process will be daily logging by staff with a weekly summary report from unit managers.",
            "mentions": [
              66412
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D3"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "white_check_mark",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M33",
            "speaker_id": 66412,
            "reply_to": "M32",
            "text": "Ok, I will update the documents A1 and A2 based on this feedback for T3.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1",
              "A2",
              "T3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M34",
            "speaker_id": 492953,
            "reply_to": "M33",
            "text": "Perfect. Let's aim to have the final versions ready by EOD tomorrow so we can start preparing the training materials (T7).",
            "mentions": [
              66412
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T7"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          }
