      {
        "thread_id": "TH3",
        "thread_goal": "Align purchasing rules and supplier arrangements with waste targets.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M35",
            "speaker_id": 332110,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Team, based on the initial data from similar units, I've analyzed the highest-waste categories. Fresh produce (leafy greens, soft fruits) and dairy are the top offenders. I've drafted revised purchasing guidelines in A3 to address this, focusing on more frequent, smaller orders. This is the core of T4. Please review and provide feedback.",
            "mentions": [
              492953,
              66412,
              412987
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3",
              "T4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "chart_with_upwards_trend",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M36",
            "speaker_id": 412987,
            "reply_to": "M35",
            "text": "This is excellent analysis. More frequent deliveries of produce makes perfect sense. It aligns with a 'fresh-first' kitchen philosophy and reduces spoilage risk. The guidelines in A3 look solid. This will require tight coordination with head chefs on their daily prep lists.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M37",
            "speaker_id": 66412,
            "reply_to": "M35",
            "text": "Will smaller orders increase our delivery costs? We have a constraint of no overall cost increase.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M38",
            "speaker_id": 332110,
            "reply_to": "M37",
            "text": "That's a key risk. However, the savings from reduced spoilage should significantly outweigh any marginal increase in delivery fees. I've run a preliminary model showing a net saving of 3-5% on those categories. Also, for T5, I'm already in talks with our main produce supplier, 'FreshDirect Logistics', who are open to daily drops at no extra charge if we give them a weekly volume estimate. I've logged this in A6.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T5",
              "A6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "heavy_dollar_sign",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M39",
            "speaker_id": 492953,
            "reply_to": "M38",
            "text": "Proactive work on the supplier negotiation, that's great to see. It de-risks the entire approach. Are there any other key suppliers we need to engage?",
            "mentions": [
              332110
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M40",
            "speaker_id": 332110,
            "reply_to": "M39",
            "text": "Yes. Our primary dairy supplier, 'County Dairy', is less flexible due to their fixed delivery routes. Our bakery supplier is the same. I propose we prioritize 'FreshDirect Logistics' (produce) and 'Prime Meats' (proteins) for T5 negotiations first, as they represent the highest cost and highest waste items. We can tackle dairy and bakery in a second phase. I've prioritized them in A6.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T5",
              "A6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M41",
            "speaker_id": 61317,
            "reply_to": "M40",
            "text": "We need to maintain good relationships with our suppliers.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M42",
            "speaker_id": 492953,
            "reply_to": "M40",
            "text": "That sounds like a smart, phased approach. Let's make a decision on that. Decision: We will prioritize negotiations with 'FreshDirect Logistics' and 'Prime Meats' for more flexible delivery terms first.",
            "mentions": [
              332110
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D6"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "white_check_mark",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M43",
            "speaker_id": 412987,
            "reply_to": "M35",
            "text": "Back to A3, the guidelines are clear. We should include a small section on 'smart substitutions' for chefs, e.g., if a specific soft fruit isn't looking great on delivery, they are empowered to refuse it and use a different menu-approved fruit. This avoids waste from poor quality deliveries.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M44",
            "speaker_id": 332110,
            "reply_to": "M43",
            "text": "Excellent point. I'll add a section on 'Receiving & Quality Control' to A3 incorporating that. It empowers the kitchen staff and protects us from paying for subpar product. I can have the revised A3 ready in an hour.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M45",
            "speaker_id": 492953,
            "reply_to": "M44",
            "text": "With that change, I think we're ready to approve the new rules for the pilot. Any final concerns?",
            "mentions": [
              66412,
              412987
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M46",
            "speaker_id": 66412,
            "reply_to": "M45",
            "text": "No, it sounds ok.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M47",
            "speaker_id": 492953,
            "reply_to": "M45",
            "text": "Great. Decision: The revised purchasing rules outlined in A3, including the new section on quality control, are approved for use in the pilot units.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "white_check_mark",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M48",
            "speaker_id": 332110,
            "reply_to": "M47",
            "text": "Understood. I will finalize A3 and continue with the supplier negotiations for T5.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3",
              "T5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          }
        ],
        "thread_outcome": {
