      {
        "thread_id": "TH4",
        "thread_goal": "Define menu, sales tactics, and communication plan for the pilot.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M49",
            "speaker_id": 412987,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi all, I've drafted the Menu and Sales Playbook (A4) for our pilot. It identifies several high-margin items that use ingredients with longer shelf lives or utilize cross-product components, which naturally reduces waste. This is the first pass at T6. I've also included some simple upsell scripts for staff. Feedback is welcome.",
            "mentions": [
              492953,
              66412,
              332110
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4",
              "T6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M50",
            "speaker_id": 332110,
            "reply_to": "M49",
            "text": "This is great, I've cross-referenced the ingredient list with my high-waste analysis. The 'Roasted Root Vegetable Medley' and the 'Hearty Lentil Soup' are perfect examples – they use produce that is less perishable than leafy greens. This directly supports our purchasing adjustments.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M51",
            "speaker_id": 492953,
            "reply_to": "M49",
            "text": "This looks very promising. How do we ensure the sales team is motivated to push these specific items? This ties into T12 on sales incentives.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T12"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M52",
            "speaker_id": 412987,
            "reply_to": "M51",
            "text": "Good question. For the pilot, I suggest we avoid a complex change to the commission structure. Instead, we can run a simple contest: the server who sells the most 'low-waste special' items each week gets a small bonus. It's easy to track and communicate. We can evaluate a more permanent incentive change (T12) after the pilot.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T12"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "trophy",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M53",
            "speaker_id": 66412,
            "reply_to": "M49",
            "text": "We need to train the staff on this. I can start working on the A5 training deck. Should I just copy the playbook into slides?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M54",
            "speaker_id": 412987,
            "reply_to": "M53",
            "text": "Let's make A5 more interactive. We should focus on role-playing the upsell scripts rather than just presenting slides. I can help you structure the training session to be more of a hands-on workshop. A simple one-pager from A4 would be a better leave-behind than the full deck.",
            "mentions": [
              66412
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5",
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M55",
            "speaker_id": 61317,
            "reply_to": "M51",
            "text": "Sales incentives are important for motivation.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M56",
            "speaker_id": 492953,
            "reply_to": "M52",
            "text": "A weekly contest is a great, low-overhead way to pilot the incentive idea. Let's agree on that approach. We also need a clear internal comms plan for T10 to announce this to the pilot units. It should be positioned as a fun challenge, not a mandatory chore.",
            "mentions": [
              412987
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T10"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M57",
            "speaker_id": 412987,
            "reply_to": "M56",
            "text": "Exactly. I've drafted a short, upbeat announcement for T10 that the unit managers can share during their pre-shift huddles. I'll share it here shortly. It frames the program around quality, freshness, and reducing our environmental impact, with the contest as a fun bonus.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T10"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M58",
            "speaker_id": 492953,
            "reply_to": "M57",
            "text": "Perfect. So, let's decide. Decision: We will use a weekly sales contest for the pilot as the incentive adjustment, and the internal communication will focus on a positive, team-challenge framing.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D8"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "white_check_mark",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M59",
            "speaker_id": 332110,
