            "speaker_id": 297089,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi team, welcome to the channel for the 'Cross-Department Protocol for High-Risk Detainee Health Monitoring' project. The main goal is to create a clear, standard process to improve safety and coordination. I've started mapping the current process for T1, and the first draft is in A1. Could everyone take a look and share your thoughts on the main gaps or pain points you see today?",
            "mentions": [
              504576,
              6456,
              19315,
              444619
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1",
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M2",
            "speaker_id": 504576,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "Thanks. Looking at A1, the biggest issue is the handover between shifts. Information is often passed verbally and gets lost. We also don't have a standard way to flag a detainee who seems 'off' but isn't showing obvious medical symptoms. It's mostly based on gut feeling right now.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "heavy_plus_sign",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 6456,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "That's a key point. Translating that 'gut feeling' into simple, observable indicators will be the focus of T2. The lack of a common vocabulary is a classic risk in these situations.",
            "mentions": [
              504576
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 19315,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "Good start. Just to be clear on scope, are we focusing on all units, or just the maximum security wing to begin with? And does this apply to all detainees or only those with pre-existing conditions?",
