            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 297089,
            "reply_to": "M4",
            "text": "Great question. The project brief suggests a broad rollout, but starting with a specific scope for the pilot makes sense. My suggestion is we design the protocol to be applicable to all detainees upon intake and during routine checks, but we pilot it in one or two specific units first. Let's say the general population and the short-stay unit, as they have high turnover. Does that sound right?",
            "mentions": [
              504576,
              19315
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D1"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M6",
            "speaker_id": 504576,
            "reply_to": "M5",
            "text": "Yes, that works. General population and short-stay cover most of our common scenarios. Maximum security has its own complexities we can tackle later.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
