      {
        "thread_id": "TH3",
        "thread_goal": "Lock in KPI set, targets, and reporting cadence for the dashboard.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M30",
            "speaker_id": 4315,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi all, for T5, I have drafted the Quality KPI Dictionary and a mock-up of the dashboard. Please see A3 for the details. I'd like to get your feedback on the proposed KPIs and reporting structure before we start the build for T10.",
            "mentions": [
              436982
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3",
              "T5",
              "T10"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M31",
            "speaker_id": 436982,
            "reply_to": "M30",
            "text": "Thanks, reviewing A3 now. The list of KPIs seems to cover the key areas. I do have a question about the definition for 'First Pass Yield'. It's a critical metric, but sites often measure it differently. We need to be very specific on whether this is pre- or post-rework to ensure we get clean, comparable data.",
            "mentions": [
              4315
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M32",
            "speaker_id": 4315,
            "reply_to": "M31",
            "text": "That's a very good point. I hadn't specified that. What is the standard best practice here?",
            "mentions": [
              436982
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M33",
            "speaker_id": 436982,
            "reply_to": "M32",
            "text": "The standard approach is to measure it before any form of rework or repair. This gives a true picture of the initial quality of the process. I can add a precise, unambiguous definition to the dictionary in A3.",
            "mentions": [
              4315
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M34",
            "speaker_id": 4315,
            "reply_to": "M33",
            "text": "Please do. That clarity is essential. With that clarification, are we happy to lock in this list of 5 core KPIs for our cross-site reporting? This would be our decision D5.",
            "mentions": [
              436982
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M35",
            "speaker_id": 436982,
            "reply_to": "M34",
            "text": "Yes, the other definitions are clear. This is a strong, manageable set of core KPIs to start with. I agree.",
            "mentions": [
              4315
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "white_check_mark",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M36",
            "speaker_id": 4315,
            "reply_to": "M35",
            "text": "Great. Now for the reporting cadence and owners, also in A3. I've proposed that site supervisors own the data entry and that all KPIs are reported weekly. Any concerns?",
            "mentions": [
              436982
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M37",
            "speaker_id": 436982,
            "reply_to": "M36",
            "text": "Weekly cadence and supervisor ownership make sense for operational metrics. My only thought is on 'Customer Complaints'. That data can be laggy and sporadic. A weekly report might jump around a lot. Would a monthly reporting cycle for that specific KPI be more stable and meaningful?",
            "mentions": [
              4315
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M38",
            "speaker_id": 4315,
            "reply_to": "M37",
            "text": "I'd prefer to keep the reporting action consistent for the supervisors - one time a week for everything. What if we still have them enter the data weekly, but on the dashboard we display it as a month-to-date figure? That way the action is simple, but the view is stable.",
            "mentions": [
              436982
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M39",
            "speaker_id": 436982,
            "reply_to": "M38",
            "text": "That's a good solution. It balances simplicity for the data owners with a stable view for management. I can add that display logic to the dashboard spec for T10.",
            "mentions": [
              4315
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T10"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M40",
            "speaker_id": 4315,
            "reply_to": "M39",
            "text": "Perfect. Let's lock that in as D6: We confirm a weekly reporting cadence with site supervisors as data owners for all KPIs. The 'Customer Complaints' KPI will be displayed as a month-to-date value. Agreed?",
            "mentions": [
              436982
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D6"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M41",
            "speaker_id": 436982,
            "reply_to": "M40",
            "text": "Agreed.",
            "mentions": [
              4315
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M42",
            "speaker_id": 4315,
            "reply_to": "M41",
            "text": "Excellent. D5 and D6 are now closed. @436982 please update A3 with the FPY definition and the display logic for complaints. I will finalize the targets with the Operations Manager this week.",
            "mentions": [
              436982
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
