            "msg_id": "M58",
            "speaker_id": 436982,
            "reply_to": "M57",
            "text": "Thanks for putting this together. It's great to see the data coming in. I'm reading through A8 now.",
            "mentions": [
              4315
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A8"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M59",
            "speaker_id": 4315,
            "reply_to": "M58",
            "text": "The good news is that most KPIs are trending positively. However, I've noticed a recurring issue logged in A8: 'Incorrect Form Usage' seems to be a common, low-level error at two sites. Any initial thoughts on a root cause?",
            "mentions": [
              436982
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A8"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M60",
            "speaker_id": 436982,
            "reply_to": "M59",
            "text": "I saw that too and reached out to one of the supervisors. It turns out the main link on their local intranet page was still pointing to an old version of the form. The SOP itself is correct, but their shortcut wasn't updated. It's likely the same issue at the other site.",
            "mentions": [
              4315
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M61",
            "speaker_id": 4315,
            "reply_to": "M60",
            "text": "Ah, a classic broken link problem. That's an easy fix. Can you coordinate with the site admins to get those updated?",
            "mentions": [
              436982
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M62",
            "speaker_id": 436982,
            "reply_to": "M61",
            "text": "I'm already on it. This also suggests an improvement for our process. I think we should update the Site Supervisor Checklist (A5) to include a pre-go-live step to 'Validate all local intranet links to quality documents'.",
            "mentions": [
              4315
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M63",
            "speaker_id": 4315,
            "reply_to": "M62",
            "text": "That's a great idea for preventing this in the future. Let's add that to the improvement backlog.",
            "mentions": [
              436982
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M64",
            "speaker_id": 436982,
            "reply_to": "M63",
            "text": "Speaking of checklists, I'm working on the quick-reference guide for supervisors (T12). Looking at the feedback in A8 and our risk register (A6), it seems there's still some minor confusion on the precise KPI definitions. I think it would be valuable to add a one-line definition for each KPI directly onto that checklist.",
            "mentions": [
              4315
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A6",
              "A8",
              "T12"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M65",
            "speaker_id": 4315,
            "reply_to": "M64",
            "text": "Yes, absolutely. Reinforcing the definitions at the point of use is a smart move. Please add that to the scope for T12.",
            "mentions": [
              436982
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T12"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
