            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "chart_with_upwards_trend",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M42",
            "speaker_id": 73292,
            "reply_to": "M41",
            "text": "I've noticed that too. The triage rule we set in D3 is sending some relatively quick tasks to the complex queue. For example, 'account balance printout with signature' is technically complex because it needs a signature, but it only takes a minute. It's backing up people who need to discuss loans or open accounts.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D3"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M43",
            "speaker_id": 252240,
            "reply_to": "M42",
            "text": "Yes, I had a few of those. The customers were not happy about waiting in the 'long' line for something so fast.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M44",
            "speaker_id": 455770,
            "reply_to": "M42",
            "text": "That's excellent, specific feedback. It sounds like we need to refine our triage rule. What if we amend D3 to be: 'Quick transactions are <3 minutes AND either require no signature OR only require a standard transaction signature (not new account paperwork)'?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
