      {
        "thread_id": "TH2",
        "thread_goal": "Define and agree on supplier qualification and cold-chain requirements.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M19",
            "speaker_id": 23046,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi team, I've put together the first draft of the Supplier Qualification matrix (A2) for our inbound materials, covering T2. Please review and provide feedback so we can finalize the requirements.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2",
              "T2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M20",
            "speaker_id": 8402,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "Thanks @23046. Looking at A2, under 'Documentation', it just says 'Quality Certification'. Can we be more specific? Are we talking about GFSI-benchmarked standards like BRC or SQF? We need to be precise here.",
            "mentions": [
              23046
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M21",
            "speaker_id": 523303,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "Good point. Also, for high-risk raw materials, we should require a Certificate of Analysis (CoA) with each shipment that includes specific microbiological testing results. I don't see that listed.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "heavy_plus_sign",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M22",
            "speaker_id": 23046,
            "reply_to": "M20",
            "text": "Ok, good feedback. I'll add GFSI certification as the standard and a requirement for CoAs for all suppliers. That will make it stronger.",
            "mentions": [
              8402,
              523303
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M23",
            "speaker_id": 523303,
            "reply_to": "M22",
            "text": "Just to clarify, @23046, the CoA with micro results is only essential for the high-risk ingredient suppliers. Applying it to packaging suppliers, for example, would be overkill and might cause issues with procurement.",
            "mentions": [
              23046
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M24",
            "speaker_id": 23046,
            "reply_to": "M23",
            "text": "Ah, right. Got it. High-risk only. I'll correct that. Thanks.",
            "mentions": [
              523303
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M25",
            "speaker_id": 8402,
            "reply_to": "M24",
            "text": "Okay, so with those changes, I think we can agree on the minimum requirements. Let's make that decision D3.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D3"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M26",
            "speaker_id": 23046,
            "reply_to": "M25",
            "text": "Great. Now for the cold-chain part of T2. For the pilot, I propose we have drivers perform manual temperature checks at departure and arrival and log them. It's simple and low-cost.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M27",
            "speaker_id": 8402,
            "reply_to": "M26",
            "text": "I'm not sure that's enough. What happens during transit? A manual check won't show us if there was a temperature deviation mid-journey. We should really be using continuous temperature data loggers in the shipments.",
            "mentions": [
              23046
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "thinking_face",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M28",
            "speaker_id": 23046,
            "reply_to": "M27",
            "text": "Data loggers will add cost and complexity to the process defined in T7. We'd have to manage getting them back from the facility too. Is it really necessary for the pilot?",
            "mentions": [
              8402
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T7"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M29",
            "speaker_id": 523303,
            "reply_to": "M28",
            "text": "@8402 is right. For a food-grade facility, demonstrating an unbroken cold chain is non-negotiable. We need the data loggers. We can use single-use loggers to avoid the return logistics hassle. The risk of not having this data is too high, we should add it to the risk register A7.",
            "mentions": [
              8402,
              23046
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A7"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "heavy_check_mark",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M30",
            "speaker_id": 23046,
            "reply_to": "M29",
            "text": "Okay, point taken. Single-use loggers it is. I'll update the requirements and add the risk to A7 as part of T11.",
            "mentions": [
              523303
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A7",
              "T11"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M31",
            "speaker_id": 8402,
            "reply_to": "M30",
            "text": "Excellent. So we've also decided on the monitoring approach for the cold chain. That's D4.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D4"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M32",
            "speaker_id": 523303,
            "reply_to": "M31",
            "text": "To recap: \n1. Supplier requirements (D3) are agreed: GFSI certification is the standard, and CoAs with micro data are required for high-risk suppliers.\n2. Cold-chain monitoring (D4) will be done using single-use data loggers for all pilot shipments.\n@23046 will update A2 accordingly.",
            "mentions": [
              23046
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D3",
              "D4"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "clap",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M33",
            "speaker_id": 23046,
            "reply_to": "M32",
            "text": "Will do. I'll have the revised A2 sent out by EOD.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          }
        ],
        "thread_outcome": {
          "decisions_made": [
            "D3",
            "D4"
          ],
          "next_steps": [
            {
              "task_id": "T2",
              "owner_id": 23046,
              "when": "EOD"
            },
            {
              "task_id": "T11",
