      {
        "thread_id": "TH3",
        "thread_goal": "Consolidate environmental and biological risk controls into design and SOPs.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M34",
            "speaker_id": 523303,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "All, I've completed the initial environmental and biological assessment (T5) and have shared the draft report A5. Key findings include potential for pest entry near the loading docks and a risk of airborne contaminants from a nearby field. I've proposed some mitigations in the report for discussion.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5",
              "T5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M35",
            "speaker_id": 8402,
            "reply_to": "M34",
            "text": "Thanks for this. This is very important. For the pest risk, we need to add a specific procedure to our SOPs in A6. I'll draft something for inspecting all incoming shipments at the dock before they enter the warehouse.",
            "mentions": [
              523303
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M36",
            "speaker_id": 89804,
            "reply_to": "M34",
            "text": "The report A5 mentions installing air curtains at the dock doors. That's a design change. It's possible, but it will have a cost and schedule impact. We need to approve that quickly if we're going to do it.",
            "mentions": [
              523303
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M37",
            "speaker_id": 45634,
            "reply_to": "M34",
            "text": "What about landscaping? Can we plant some kind of barrier trees to help with the airborne dust from the field?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M38",
            "speaker_id": 523303,
            "reply_to": "M37",
            "text": "Landscaping could help long-term, but it won't be effective for the pilot in 30 days. The most reliable control for airborne contaminants is enhanced air filtration (HEPA filters) in the HVAC system for sensitive production areas. This, along with the air curtains @89804 mentioned, would be my primary recommendation.",
            "mentions": [
              89804,
              45634
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M39",
            "speaker_id": 89804,
            "reply_to": "M38",
            "text": "Upgrading to HEPA filters is a significant change to the HVAC spec. I'm not sure our current units can even take them. I need to check with the supplier. This could be a big problem.",
            "mentions": [
              523303
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "warning",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M40",
            "speaker_id": 8402,
            "reply_to": "M39",
            "text": "This sounds serious. We can't operate without controlling airborne contamination. What's the alternative?",
            "mentions": [
              89804
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M41",
            "speaker_id": 523303,
            "reply_to": "M40",
            "text": "Let's not panic. @89804, please check on the HEPA filter compatibility ASAP. If it's not possible, we can look at localized air purifiers in the critical zones as a temporary measure, but it's not ideal. The best solution is integrated HVAC filtration and air curtains. Let's agree that these design changes are required, and figure out the implementation. This is decision D6.",
            "mentions": [
              89804
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D6"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M42",
            "speaker_id": 89804,
            "reply_to": "M41",
            "text": "Ok, I'll check. I agree we need to do something. I'll confirm by tomorrow morning.",
            "mentions": [
              523303
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M43",
            "speaker_id": 523303,
            "reply_to": "M41",
            "text": "Thank you. Now, regarding the ongoing environmental monitoring plan for T10. Based on the assessment, I propose weekly air and surface sampling at 5 critical points in the production area, and monthly water testing. The details are in A5.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5",
              "T10"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M44",
            "speaker_id": 8402,
            "reply_to": "M43",
            "text": "That sounds like a lot of testing. Is weekly really necessary? It will be expensive. Can we do it monthly to start?",
            "mentions": [
              523303
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M45",
            "speaker_id": 523303,
            "reply_to": "M44",
            "text": "For a new facility, weekly is the standard to establish a baseline and prove our cleaning and air handling systems are effective. We can potentially reduce the frequency after we have 3-6 months of stable data showing we are in control. For go-live, I strongly recommend we stick to weekly.",
            "mentions": [
              8402
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M46",
            "speaker_id": 8402,
            "reply_to": "M45",
            "text": "Okay, that makes sense. I'm convinced. Let's approve the proposed monitoring plan. That's D5.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M47",
            "speaker_id": 45634,
            "reply_to": "M41",
            "text": "So I need to update the drawings to include air curtains?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M48",
            "speaker_id": 523303,
            "reply_to": "M47",
            "text": "Yes, @45634. Please proceed with that. To summarize: \n1. We've agreed on the environmental monitoring plan (D5). \n2. We've agreed to implement air curtains and enhanced air filtration as critical design changes (D6), pending feasibility check from @89804. \n3. @8402 will update the SOPs in A6 for pest control as part of T6.",
            "mentions": [
              45634,
              89804,
              8402
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A6",
              "T6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5",
              "D6"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "rocket",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "thread_outcome": {
          "decisions_made": [
            "D5",
            "D6"
          ],
          "next_steps": [
            {
              "task_id": "T6",
              "owner_id": 8402,
              "when": "this week"
            },
            {
              "task_id": "T10",
              "owner_id": 523303,
              "when": "this week"
            },
            {
              "task_id": "T4",
              "owner_id": 89804,
              "when": "tomorrow"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "thread_id": "TH4",
        "thread_goal": "Lock the commissioning, validation, and pilot go-live plan.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M49",
            "speaker_id": 89804,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Team, please find the draft commissioning plan (T9) and readiness checklist (A4). I've tried to capture all the main systems. Let me know your feedback so we can get this finalized.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4",
              "T9"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M50",
            "speaker_id": 23046,
            "reply_to": "M49",
            "text": "Thanks. I've reviewed the go-live checklist A8 that feeds into this. It's missing a few things for supply chain: supplier final approvals, transport partner readiness, and warehouse system integration testing. I can send you a list of about 10 items to add.",
            "mentions": [
              89804
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A8"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M51",
            "speaker_id": 8402,
            "reply_to": "M49",
            "text": "Looking at the validation section. It seems a bit light. We need to run validation tests for every single process step defined in the flow map A1. For example, I don't see a test protocol for the internal transfer of intermediate products.",
            "mentions": [
              89804
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M52",
            "speaker_id": 523303,
            "reply_to": "M51",
            "text": "I agree we need to be thorough, but testing every single step might be excessive and delay us. We should focus validation on the Critical Control Points identified in A1. For microbiological validation, we need to test the cleaning procedures after a full production run, which I see is in the plan. That's good.",
            "mentions": [
              8402
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M53",
            "speaker_id": 89804,
            "reply_to": "M51",
            "text": "I wasn't sure how detailed to make the validation part. I can add more, but I'll need your input on the specific test protocols for T9.",
            "mentions": [
              8402
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T9"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M54",
            "speaker_id": 8402,
            "reply_to": "M52",
            "text": "Okay, focusing on CCPs is a reasonable compromise. I will work with you @89804 to detail those specific protocols for the plan.",
            "mentions": [
              89804,
              523303
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M55",
            "speaker_id": 45634,
            "reply_to": "M49",
            "text": "The plan should also include a formal handover from the construction team to the operations team, with sign-off on the as-built drawings.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M56",
            "speaker_id": 89804,
            "reply_to": "M55",
            "text": "Yes, that's part of the 'Facility Acceptance' line item in A4, but I can make it more explicit.",
            "mentions": [
              45634
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M57",
            "speaker_id": 8402,
            "reply_to": "M56",
            "text": "Okay, a lot of good inputs. Let's get to a decision. Can we approve the commissioning schedule and responsibilities as laid out, with the commitment to add the details we just discussed?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D7"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M58",
            "speaker_id": 23046,
            "reply_to": "M57",
            "text": "I'm good with that, as long as my supply chain readiness items are added to the go-live checklist A8.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A8"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M59",
            "speaker_id": 523303,
            "reply_to": "M57",
            "text": "Yes, I approve. The timeline looks aggressive but achievable if we stay on track.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "heavy_check_mark",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M60",
            "speaker_id": 8402,
            "reply_to": "M59",
            "text": "Great, that's D7 confirmed. Now for D8: what are the final criteria and target date for pilot go-live readiness? The plan says 'end of month'. Can we be more specific? I propose we target Day 28 for 100% completion of the go-live checklist A8, giving us a 2-day buffer.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A8"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D8"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M61",
            "speaker_id": 89804,
            "reply_to": "M60",
            "text": "Day 28 is tight, but it's a clear target. I can work with that.",
            "mentions": [
              8402
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M62",
            "speaker_id": 23046,
            "reply_to": "M60",
            "text": "Works for me. The criteria is 100% on the checklist. Clear and simple.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M63",
            "speaker_id": 8402,
            "reply_to": "M62",
            "text": "Excellent. Decisions are locked. To recap:\n1. Commissioning schedule and responsibilities are approved (D7). The plan will be updated with validation protocols for CCPs, explicit handover steps, and supply chain readiness items.\n2. Pilot go-live readiness criteria is 100% completion of the T12 checklist (A8) by Day 28 (D8).",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A8",
              "T12"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D7",
              "D8"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "clap",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M64",
            "speaker_id": 89804,
            "reply_to": "M63",
            "text": "Understood. I'll start making the updates to T9 and A4.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T9",
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          }
        ],
        "thread_outcome": {
