            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "Thanks for starting. From a quality perspective, the biggest issue is inconsistency. Each shift seems to have its own 'version' of the process, especially around what data is captured on paper vs. the EHR. This leads to gaps and makes auditing impossible. We have no standard to measure against.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "heavy_plus_sign",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 438229,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "Exactly. I've noticed some front-desk staff use the old paper forms while others type directly into the system. It also depends on how busy it is. When there's a rush, things get missed. We need one clear process.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 313168,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "From the nursing side, the main problem is getting incomplete information from the front desk. Sometimes we have to ask the patient the same questions again, which is frustrating for them and slows down triage. Also, there's no clear rule for when to escalate a patient who seems to be getting worse in the waiting room.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "eyes",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 196511,
            "reply_to": "M4",
            "text": "That escalation point is critical. It's a patient experience issue too. If a patient feels they aren't being monitored properly after check-in, their anxiety goes way up. The handoff between the admin and clinical teams feels like the biggest gap.",
            "mentions": [
              313168
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "point_up",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M6",
            "speaker_id": 435140,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "This is all very helpful for thinking about the training materials. Just to be clear, are we redesigning the entire process from the moment a patient walks in, or are some parts, like appointment verification, staying the same?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M7",
            "speaker_id": 189450,
            "reply_to": "M6",
            "text": "Good question. I think for this first rollout, we should keep the initial appointment verification step as-is. The focus should be on standardizing the intake forms, consent, and the clinical triage protocol itself. We can tackle other parts later. Does that sound right to everyone?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D2"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M8",
            "speaker_id": 437517,
            "reply_to": "M7",
            "text": "Agreed. Let's focus the scope. Based on the pain points mentioned, I propose our main objectives should be: 1. Reduce check-in to triage time by 15%, 2. Achieve 95% data consistency between paper/EHR, and 3. Have zero escalations missed per week. We need measurable goals.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "chart_with_upwards_trend",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M9",
            "speaker_id": 313168,
            "reply_to": "M8",
            "text": "Those numbers sound a bit high. How will we measure the time exactly?",
            "mentions": [
              437517
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M10",
            "speaker_id": 437517,
            "reply_to": "M9",
            "text": "We can set up a simple time-logging sheet during the pilot. It's just a target to aim for. We can adjust it based on the pilot data.",
            "mentions": [
              313168
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M11",
            "speaker_id": 189450,
            "reply_to": "M8",
            "text": "I like having clear metrics. Let's formalize that. So, we're agreeing on two key things here. First, our success metrics are reducing wait times, improving data quality, and ensuring patient safety via clear escalation. Second, we're confirming that the initial appointment verification process will remain unchanged for now.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D1",
              "D2"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "white_check_mark",
                "count": 4
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M12",
            "speaker_id": 196511,
            "reply_to": "M11",
            "text": "Sounds good. That gives us a clear scope.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M13",
            "speaker_id": 438229,
            "reply_to": "M11",
            "text": "Okay, I'll start pulling together the different paper forms we use now to help with the T1 mapping.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
