        "thread_id": "TH2",
        "thread_goal": "Review and finalise the early identification and referral protocol and observation checklist.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M19",
            "speaker_id": 361403,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi all, following on from our discussion about procedures, I've drafted the Early Identification and Referral Protocol (A2) as part of T2. It's in the shared drive. Could the EYTAs in particular please review it against current school practices? I want to make sure it aligns with existing kindergarten procedures as per T11.",
            "mentions": [
              499701,
              511446,
              350111
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2",
              "T2",
              "T11"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M20",
            "speaker_id": 499701,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "Thanks for sharing this so quickly. I've read through A2. The flow is logical, but I have a concern about the data sharing consent form on page 3. It feels a bit heavy for an initial conversation with a parent. Could we simplify it to a verbal consent model for the initial stages, with written consent required only if we proceed to a formal referral? This would align better with how we build trust with families.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "thinking_face",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M21",
            "speaker_id": 511446,
            "reply_to": "M20",
            "text": "I agree with @499701. A big form upfront could be a barrier. A two-stage consent process makes sense. The protocol should be very clear about what information is shared at each stage.",
            "mentions": [
              499701
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M22",
            "speaker_id": 361403,
            "reply_to": "M20",
            "text": "That's a great point about building trust. I can definitely adjust that. A two-stage consent process is fine as long as we're explicit about the triggers for written consent. I'll revise that section in A2.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M23",
            "speaker_id": 427511,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "What if the parents say no?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M24",
            "speaker_id": 361403,
            "reply_to": "M23",
            "text": "If parents don't consent, we can't share information, and the joint part of the process stops. We would continue with our standard in-school support. The protocol will make that clear. The only exception is a statutory safeguarding concern, which follows a different path anyway.",
            "mentions": [
              427511
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M25",
            "speaker_id": 499701,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "Also, let's look at the Classroom Observation Checklist (A3) for T3. I've put a draft version in the folder. The goal was to keep it completable in under 5 minutes. Can you all take a look and see if the indicators are clear and practical?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3",
              "T3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M26",
            "speaker_id": 511446,
            "reply_to": "M25",
            "text": "The checklist A3 looks great. It's simple and covers the key areas without being overwhelming. How often are we thinking it should be used?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M27",
            "speaker_id": 499701,
            "reply_to": "M26",
            "text": "I'd suggest it's not a routine weekly thing for all children, as that would be too much. It should be used when a concern is first noted, and then perhaps weekly for a few weeks for any child who is being actively monitored through the new protocol. Does that sound reasonable?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M28",
            "speaker_id": 350111,
            "reply_to": "M27",
            "text": "Yes, using it only when we have a concern is better. It will be too much work otherwise.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M29",
            "speaker_id": 361403,
            "reply_to": "M27",
            "text": "That frequency makes sense. It provides a good baseline and then tracks progress without creating a huge administrative burden. The indicators on A3 are relevant from a social work perspective too.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M30",
            "speaker_id": 511446,
            "reply_to": "M29",
            "text": "Okay, let's lock in that decision. The final version of the classroom observation checklist (A3) is agreed, to be used upon initial concern and then weekly for monitored children.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D4"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "white_check_mark",
