      {
        "thread_id": "TH3",
        "thread_goal": "Define classroom support routines and align them with school procedures and workload.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M34",
            "speaker_id": 511446,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi team, I've drafted some ideas for the Standardised Classroom Support Routines (A4) as part of T6. The document lists a few practical strategies like 'visual timetables' and 'buddy system'. Are these realistic to implement without overloading staff?",
            "mentions": [
              499701,
              350111
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4",
              "T6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M35",
            "speaker_id": 499701,
            "reply_to": "M34",
            "text": "Thanks for starting this. These are good, and many are already part of good practice. To avoid overload, we should frame them as a 'menu' of options that teachers can choose from, rather than a mandatory checklist for every child. We could group them into categories like 'Social & Emotional', 'Learning Support', etc.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M36",
            "speaker_id": 350111,
            "reply_to": "M34",
            "text": "I like the 'buddy system' idea. We use that sometimes and it works well. A 'quiet corner' is also a good one for children who get overwhelmed.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M37",
            "speaker_id": 361403,
            "reply_to": "M35",
            "text": "The 'menu' approach is smart. It empowers the teaching staff. From a social-emotional perspective, having options like a 'quiet corner' or 'check-in charts' are excellent for helping children with self-regulation. These all support social-emotional needs well.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M38",
            "speaker_id": 427511,
            "reply_to": "M34",
            "text": "Do we need to write down every time we use one of these?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M39",
            "speaker_id": 511446,
            "reply_to": "M38",
            "text": "Good question. I don't think so. The idea is that the chosen strategies for a specific child would be noted in their support plan, but we wouldn't log every single instance. It's about the routine, not the paperwork. This links to our feedback process in T10 - if a strategy isn't working, staff can flag it during the check-ins described in A8.",
            "mentions": [
              427511
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T10",
              "A8"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M40",
            "speaker_id": 499701,
            "reply_to": "M39",
            "text": "Exactly. Let's finalize the list. How about we go with these six: 1. Visual Timetable, 2. Buddy System, 3. Quiet Corner, 4. Emotion Check-in Chart, 5. Task Chunking, 6. Positive Reinforcement notes. That's a robust but manageable set.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M41",
            "speaker_id": 511446,
            "reply_to": "M40",
            "text": "That's a great set. I'll formalize the decision: The selected classroom support strategies are Visual Timetable, Buddy System, Quiet Corner, Emotion Check-in Chart, Task Chunking, and Positive Reinforcement notes.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "white_check_mark",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M42",
            "speaker_id": 350111,
            "reply_to": "M41",
            "text": "Sounds good.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M43",
            "speaker_id": 499701,
            "reply_to": "M41",
            "text": "Now, how do we make sure staff can easily access this? A one-page guideline in our shared project folder seems best. We can link to it from the main protocol document.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M44",
            "speaker_id": 511446,
            "reply_to": "M43",
            "text": "Agreed. Let's make that the final decision here. The support routines will be documented as a one-page guideline (A4) stored in the shared drive and linked from the main protocol.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
