            "speaker_id": 67957,
            "reply_to": "M50",
            "text": "From my experience in labs, a 'near-miss' is also critical to log – something that could have caused an issue but didn't. For example, if I almost grabbed the wrong cleaning bottle. For this pilot, maybe we can have three simple categories in A5: 1) Incident (e.g., skin reaction), 2) Near-Miss (e.g., almost slipped), 3) Observation/Feedback (e.g., client question).",
