    "threads": [
      {
        "thread_id": "TH1",
        "thread_goal": "Align on current workflow, main pain points and pilot scope for one aisle.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M1",
            "speaker_id": 331660,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi team, let's kick off the replenishment pilot. To start, can everyone briefly describe the current backroom-to-shelf process from their perspective? We need to map it out for T1. What are the biggest headaches right now?",
            "mentions": [
              36271,
              37492,
              300804,
              321832
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M2",
            "speaker_id": 36271,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "From my side, when the truck arrives it's a bit of a free-for-all. We unload pallets and they sit wherever there's space. Then we have to move them again to get to the right stock for the aisle. Lots of double handling.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 321832,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "Agree with that. By the time the trolley gets to the aisle, it's often mixed products. For shelf fillers, it means sorting on the shop floor, which blocks customers. And we often find expired stock hidden at the back of the shelf because it wasn't rotated properly.",
            "mentions": [
              36271
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 37492,
